What upstream lacks (hermes-agent, apps/desktop): a way to keep every web page
out of the app, and to open one only when the user clicks it. By default a
clicked link opens in the in-app Browser pane (a <webview>), the agent's
preview.open events open URLs there by themselves, the link context menu
offers "Open in in-app browser", and a page in the pane can redirect itself
anywhere; only Ctrl/middle-click or a per-device setting reach the system
browser.

This patch (Nix). Rule: a web page reaches the system browser only because
the user clicked (or typed) it; nothing opens it on its own.
  - openLink always calls openExternalLink (hermes:openExternal -> main's
    openExternalUrl -> shell.openExternal); the context menu no longer
    offers "open in app".
  - openPreview never shows an http(s) page: what reaches it with one is the
    agent's preview.open (dev servers included), so it only shows a
    bottom-right toast with the URL and an "Open in browser" button
    (strings in i18n en: preview.webPageOffer*).
    User-click callers (file tree, attachments, preview rows, contrib panes)
    use openPreviewFromClick, which opens the system browser directly.
  - inside a preview guest (an HTML file, the blank Browser) the preload
    forwards every trusted click on an http(s) link (primary or middle) to
    the system browser and cancels its in-pane navigation. The agent's
    drive_preview input (sendInputEvent) is trusted too, so while a
    preview.act runs and for 1.5 s after it or after any event it sent
    (preview-input.ts), such a link is only offered as the toast below.
  - main blocks every other navigation of a guest that is not file:,
    about: or data: (script or <meta refresh> redirects, mailto: and custom
    schemes) without opening anything, and the persist:hermes-preview
    session denies the openExternal permission (OS protocol handlers).
  - an address typed into the blank Browser's bar goes to the system browser.
  - web-page tabs persisted by an older build are dropped on restore.
  - the "Always open links in external browser" setting is hidden (moot).
File, artifact and image previews keep the pane. Sign-in (OAuth) flows call
openExternal directly and are untouched.
Tested by src/store/preview-links-external.test.ts and
electron/preview-guest-links-external.test.ts.
Left in place (dead now, removing it would grow this patch a lot): the
external-links store and its i18n keys (several upstream tests import it),
the link.openInApp i18n key; hudForcesNativeLinks and the context menu's
open-in-app items are removed (upstream's external-link.test.tsx, not run
here, still names the former).

